# Critter — optional configuration
# Local pet animation, interaction and notes need no model credentials.
# Copy to .env only when needed, then uncomment and fill the chosen settings.
# All model fields are inactive by default; do not use placeholder keys.
# Full routing and precedence: docs/configuration.md

# OpenAI-compatible API: ordinary chat, diary generation and Agent.
# Fill all three using your provider's settings; Agent also needs tool calling.
# A non-empty OPENAI_API_KEY selects this route even if the key is invalid.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_BASE=https://your-provider.example/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=your-model-id

# Anthropic API: Agent only when OPENAI_API_KEY is absent or empty.
# Ordinary chat and diaries still require a configured Claude CLI in this mode.
# CLI authentication does not replace Agent API credentials.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Claude CLI: ordinary chat and diaries when OPENAI_API_KEY is absent or empty.
# Install/configure the CLI separately; Critter looks for `claude` on PATH.
# No additional Critter variable is needed for CLI authentication.

# Optional local data directory (absolute path or ~/...).
# Unset: keep using ~/.desktop-pet-state.json; set: use <directory>/state.json.
# An explicit shell CRITTER_DATA_DIR takes precedence over this file.
# Existing data is not copied automatically; read docs/usage-and-storage.md.
# CRITTER_DATA_DIR="/absolute/path/to/critter-data"
